# ✨ Dev.to Posts Highlights! ✨

#### Here is one of the posts I am proud of for this month!

{% embed https://dev.to/francistrdev/networking-is-hard-but-easy-to-think-about-dc1 %}

_Talked about networking and how it is something we all know that is helpful for our career, but is hard to do for many reasons._



&nbsp;

&nbsp;



#### Here is the top 3 posts that I have discovered that stood out to me!

{% embed https://dev.to/codingwithjiro/the-slow-and-quiet-cognitive-atrophy-of-a-modern-software-engineer-3lbh %}

@codingwithjiro _The importance about maintaining a developer mindset in the age of AI. Also, talking about challenging yourself, asking questions, and maintaining discipline whenever you are using AI tools or not._


&nbsp;


{% embed https://dev.to/dj29/we-all-have-a-serious-work-ai-and-a-just-vibing-ai-when-did-that-happen-5fl2 %}

@dj29 _Opening a discussion about which AI do you use for specific use cases such as using one AI to do essays or another AI to do code work._


&nbsp;


{% embed https://dev.to/annavi11arrea1/sharing-dev-followers-count-on-github-profile-bj3 %}

@annavi11arrea1 _GitHub Action that shows your dev.to follower that you can put on your README.MD :)_





